WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:13.041
This video shows how to put an animation from Pixodesk SVG Animator on a web page, as a single SVG file in an iframe. There is no library, no install, and no build step.

2
00:00:14.267 --> 00:00:16.565
Let's start with the page as it is.

3
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.051
A heading, and nothing that moves yet.

4
00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:30.256
The animation comes first. Let's switch to the editor, where a football is already drawn.

5
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.229
It's a vector drawing, standing still.

6
00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:38.601
To make it move, let's switch on Auto mode.

7
00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:44.731
With Auto mode on, every change becomes a keyframe.

8
00:00:45.967 --> 00:00:49.258
Half a second in, let's drag the ball down to the floor.

9
00:00:52.367 --> 00:00:56.050
A keyframe appears on the timeline, holding the new position.

10
00:00:57.267 --> 00:00:59.383
At one second, let's bring it back up.

11
00:01:02.667 --> 00:01:06.820
Now it falls and rises again, in one second.

12
00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:14.911
A real ball speeds up as it falls, and slows down as it rises. Let's set that easing.

13
00:01:22.033 --> 00:01:26.683
Gravity easing, falling and rising, makes the bounce feel natural.

14
00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:31.035
One bounce is not enough, so let's loop the animation.

15
00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:38.653
Loop is saved with the file, so the animation repeats forever.

16
00:01:40.867 --> 00:01:45.752
The animation is ready. Let's save it as SVG, next to the page.

17
00:01:50.733 --> 00:01:55.331
The animation is written into the SVG file itself, as CSS.

18
00:01:56.567 --> 00:01:58.552
Now, back to our page.

19
00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:03.653
The SVG file is already there, next to the page.

20
00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:07.042
Let's show the file in an iframe.

21
00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:20.786
The iframe opens the SVG as its own document, and its animation runs there.

22
00:02:22.033 --> 00:02:24.332
Let's reload the page, and watch.

23
00:02:29.467 --> 00:02:34.012
There it is. The ball bounces, with no library on the page.

24
00:02:36.033 --> 00:02:44.340
So, one SVG file saved from the editor, and one iframe tag. That's all it takes, with no library and no build step.
